WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.701
-Thank you very much
for being here.

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.267
Welcome to
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.367
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:08.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.567
Let's get to some news.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.801
Well, guys, with all the
holiday travel being planned,

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.467
President Biden has proposed
new rules that would require

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:21.167
airlines to show consumers the
actual price of plane tickets,

00:00:21.167 --> 00:00:26.200
including baggage fees and other
extra costs, before they buy.

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:30.234
Yeah. Of course, the airlines
all responded by adding an

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.067
"able to see the full cost" fee.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:35.133
But besides that --
Yeah, airlines will have to show

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:36.434
all their hidden fees.

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:37.801
Right now, every
credit-card company is like,

00:00:37.801 --> 00:00:39.033
"Don't make eye contact.

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:41.634
Don't make eye contact.
He's walking right by.

00:00:41.634 --> 00:00:43.367
Don't look at him."

00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:46.400
Of course, out of spite, now the
airlines are being too honest.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.667
Today, pilots were like,
"Well, folks,

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:52.167
this turbulence is
something to worry about."

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.400
Listen to this.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.067
A new poll found that,
in a potential 2024 matchup,

00:00:58.067 --> 00:01:00.701
Biden and Trump
are essentially tied.

00:01:00.701 --> 00:01:04.000
Keep in mind the poll
has a 3-point margin of error

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.300
and a 10-point margin of
"These guys are like 80,

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.734
let's not get ahead
of ourselves."

00:01:09.734 --> 00:01:11.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.968
Well, everybody is
talking about this.

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:20.000
Rihanna just announced
that she is headlining

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:23.968
the 2023 Super Bowl
halftime show!

00:01:23.968 --> 00:01:25.968
[ Cheers and applause ]
Rihanna!

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:31.067
But it's Rihanna,
so she was like, "Wow.

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.767
This is one of the
top-10 honors of my week."

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.334
You can tell fans
are excited because at

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:38.067
the beginning of every game,
the announcer is like,

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:39.934
"And remember,
the winning team advances to

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:43.067
the Rihanna concert."

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:44.133
And it was just announced
that Apple Music

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:47.734
has replaced
Pepsi as the sponsor of

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:49.501
the Super Bowl halftime show.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.367
And just like with Pepsi,
the NFL was told,

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.501
"We don't have Spotify.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:57.000
Is Apple Music okay?"

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.901
Of course, if it rains, Rihanna
will stand under...an umbrella.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:04.534
♪♪

00:02:04.534 --> 00:02:07.267
Or she'll have to be submerged
in a bowl of rice for two days.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:10.501
Since it's Apple.
That's the way Apple...

00:02:11.767 --> 00:02:14.000
During -- Speaking of the NFL,
during yesterday's game --

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.934
I don't know if you saw this --
between the Miami Dolphins

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:17.834
and the Buffalo Bills,
Miami's punter

00:02:17.834 --> 00:02:20.300
had his kick blocked
in a pretty unfortunate way.

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:21.601
Watch this.

00:02:21.601 --> 00:02:24.701
-I don't know. This is risky.
And it was blocked.

00:02:24.701 --> 00:02:27.467
-Oh, my goodness!
Blocked, indeed.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:29.067
Let's see if we can get a...

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:32.868
Oh, it hit the personal
protector, Sherfield.

00:02:32.868 --> 00:02:35.067
-Ooh, yeah.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:36.801
The refs ruled it a safety
but said it was

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.767
very close to a sack.

00:02:38.767 --> 00:02:41.701
-Oh! Whoa!

00:02:41.701 --> 00:02:43.367
-Very close.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:49.334
♪♪

00:02:49.334 --> 00:02:51.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:58.701 --> 00:03:00.467
Well, hey, everyone,
this is very interesting.

00:03:00.467 --> 00:03:02.601
I saw that a school in Australia

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:06.300
banned a student for having
an inappropriate mullet.

00:03:08.067 --> 00:03:10.400
Good thing we don't have
any rules like that here at

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.100
"The tonight Show,"
right, Higgins?

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:15.000
-Right on, brother!

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:17.467
Can't lock down these locks.

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.567
Bottom up, homey.

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:20.801
-I hear that, brother.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:22.534
The administrators
at that school

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.934
need to take
a chill pill, brother.

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.968
-If I went to that school and
they tried to tame my mullet,

00:03:29.968 --> 00:03:31.634
you know what I'd tell them?

00:03:31.634 --> 00:03:32.901
-What?

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:36.200
-I'd tell them this, brother.

00:03:38.167 --> 00:03:40.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.067
-Rock 'n' roll, brother.
Hot damn, brother!

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:47.467
-Come on! Yeah!

00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:49.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.501 --> 00:04:01.133
I heard that grocery prices
are skyrocketing due to

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.067
a nationwide butter shortage.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.567
-Ooh!
-It's bad.

00:04:04.567 --> 00:04:06.167
At CVS, they moved
the Land O'Lakes

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:09.200
behind a locked display case.

00:04:10.868 --> 00:04:11.934
I'll be honest.

00:04:11.934 --> 00:04:13.334
Biden might have
survived the gas crisis,

00:04:13.334 --> 00:04:14.601
but there's no way in hell
he's going to make it through

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:16.133
a butter shortage -- no way.

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:21.033
Due to Hurricane Ian,
the January 6th Committee

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.968
just postponed
its public hearing

00:04:22.968 --> 00:04:24.767
that was scheduled for tomorrow.

00:04:24.767 --> 00:04:27.167
Yeah, all day, Trump was praying
for a rain delay

00:04:27.167 --> 00:04:29.033
like a pitcher facing
Aaron Judge.

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.767
He's like, "Please."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:32.467
Yep, the hearing is postponed.

00:04:32.467 --> 00:04:34.567
This morning, Trump woke up
like Kevin in "Home Alone."

00:04:34.567 --> 00:04:36.434
He's like,
"I made my hearing disappear."

00:04:36.434 --> 00:04:37.934
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.133
Some political news --
Senator Bernie Sanders said

00:04:40.133 --> 00:04:42.634
that he hasn't yet decided
whether he will run

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:45.434
for president again in 2024.

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:47.667
Yeah. People were like,
"President of what?"

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.601
Yep, Bernie
still hasn't decided.

00:04:51.601 --> 00:04:52.767
Meanwhile,
everyone else is like,

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:54.801
"How many times
do we have to decide this?

00:04:54.801 --> 00:04:56.934
No."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.934 --> 00:04:58.334
Right now, Biden is thinking,

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.367
"Please run so I look like
the hot, young stud. Please."

00:05:00.367 --> 00:05:02.467
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.467 --> 00:05:03.934
Yeah, well,
ahead of midterm elections,

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:07.133
House GOP Leader Kevin McCarthy
and other House Republicans

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.501
put out a new ad
promoting their agenda.

00:05:09.501 --> 00:05:12.167
But there was one problem --
some of the footage in the ad

00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:13.400
that was supposed to be America

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.133
was actually footage
from Russia.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:17.167
[ Laughter ]
That's real.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.434
And that wasn't
the only mistake.

00:05:18.434 --> 00:05:19.934
Take a look at this spot.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.567 --> 00:05:40.501
-Yeah, there's so many --
-Wow!

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.133
Not even close.
-Riddled.

00:05:42.133 --> 00:05:44.934
Riddled with errors.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:47.267
-Speaking of Russia,
I just heard that they announced

00:05:47.267 --> 00:05:50.133
they're boycotting
next year's Oscars.

00:05:50.133 --> 00:05:52.133
Mm, that's a tough break
for Russia's biggest movie

00:05:52.133 --> 00:05:54.834
this year, "I Actually Have
A Lot to Worry About Darling."

00:05:54.834 --> 00:05:57.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.634 --> 00:06:03.300
You guys see this last night?
NASA intentionally crashed

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:06.601
a spacecraft into an asteroid
to see if it could stop one

00:06:06.601 --> 00:06:08.901
coming towards Earth
in the future.

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.567
Go, NASA.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.567 --> 00:06:13.167
Meanwhile, the Space Force
was like, "Cool, cool.

00:06:13.167 --> 00:06:14.968
So what exactly
is our role again?

00:06:14.968 --> 00:06:16.968
Like, what -- what do we do?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.968 --> 00:06:18.734
Hey, listen to this --
I heard that the CIA

00:06:18.734 --> 00:06:21.434
just launched its own podcast.

00:06:21.434 --> 00:06:23.667
The CIA was like, "After
75 years of listening to you,

00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:26.300
now you can listen to us."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.634
Well, guys,
everyone loves TikTok,

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.100
but sometimes you just
want to skip through

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.000
the boring parts of a video
and get right to the good part.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.067
Well, it turns out you can

00:06:33.067 --> 00:06:34.234
with this new thing
that we're doing on our show.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:35.734
For instance,
if you're watching a video here,

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:36.968
you can skip this part...

00:06:36.968 --> 00:06:39.033
♪♪

00:06:39.033 --> 00:06:40.634
...and go right to this part.

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:43.000
♪♪

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:49.300
Let me give you another example.
You can skip this part...

00:06:53.534 --> 00:06:55.200
and go right to this part.

00:06:56.934 --> 00:06:57.968
[ Thuds ]

00:06:57.968 --> 00:06:59.868
[ Audience "Ohhs" ]

00:06:59.868 --> 00:07:01.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:01.868 --> 00:07:03.968
The fish tank!

00:07:03.968 --> 00:07:06.000
The final example --
you can skip this part...

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:09.801
-I'm doing a part two to
the treadmill video

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:11.601
I did just recently.

00:07:11.601 --> 00:07:13.267
-...yeah, and just go
right to this part.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:19.367
[ Laughter ]
-There you go. Perfect.

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:23.067
Just so you know
that's available.

00:07:23.067 --> 00:07:25.167
Switching gears --
ahead of the holiday season,

00:07:25.167 --> 00:07:26.501
Macy's announced plans to hire

00:07:26.501 --> 00:07:28.968
more than 40,000 new workers.

00:07:28.968 --> 00:07:31.467
So divide that between
the remaining Macy's locations,

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.467
and you have 40,000 per store.

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:35.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:38.234
Some more business news.
In an effort to fight theft,

00:07:38.234 --> 00:07:42.367
retailers like Home Depot
are now locking up items.

00:07:42.367 --> 00:07:44.567
I'm not sure I trust
Home Depot on security

00:07:44.567 --> 00:07:46.234
when they can't even
keep birds out.

00:07:46.234 --> 00:07:49.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.567 --> 00:07:52.834
Some TV news -- the other night,
there was a new --

00:07:52.834 --> 00:07:54.200
There's always birds
in Home Depot flying around.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:56.701
-Come on, there are.
"What's this bird doing in here?

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:58.234
Come on.
It's not a bird store."

00:07:58.234 --> 00:07:59.968
-Some TV news --
the other night,

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:02.400
there was an all-new episode
of "Celebrity Wheel of Fortune,"

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.968
and one of the contestants --
Snoop Dogg --

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:06.868
had a little trouble
with some of the puzzles.

00:08:06.868 --> 00:08:08.634
This is real. Check this out.

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:12.501
[ Bell dings ]
-Snoop?

00:08:12.501 --> 00:08:14.534
-"Swallowing the -- the knot"?

00:08:14.534 --> 00:08:15.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:17.133
-That --
no, that's not right.

00:08:17.133 --> 00:08:20.067
[ Bell dings ]
Snoop?

00:08:20.067 --> 00:08:21.501
-"Airport teacher."
-No.

00:08:21.501 --> 00:08:24.868
[ Bell dings ]
And Snoop?

00:08:24.868 --> 00:08:26.000
"Toilet Atlas."

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.701
[ Laughter ]
-I have no idea.

00:08:28.701 --> 00:08:31.701
[ Bell dings ]
-And it's Snoop.

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:32.968
-"Baking onions."

00:08:32.968 --> 00:08:34.100
[ Laughter ]

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.000
[ Rimshot ]

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.000
[ Applause ]

00:08:41.334 --> 00:08:43.367
-Something was baked that night.
It wasn't onions.

00:08:45.033 --> 00:08:47.467
Well, guys, this should put you
in an even better mood.

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:49.534
Today is
National Drink Beer Day.

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:52.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:52.234 --> 00:08:54.234
I understood
when some of my writers

00:08:54.234 --> 00:08:56.167
stayed home Monday and Tuesday
for Rosh Hashanah,

00:08:56.167 --> 00:08:57.200
but today was pushing it.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:58.534
It was like, "Really."

00:08:58.534 --> 00:09:00.667
Yeah, it's a day
that always starts off fun,

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:01.767
then ends with, "No, Officer,

00:09:01.767 --> 00:09:03.567
you have the right
to remain silent."

00:09:03.567 --> 00:09:04.734
[ Light laughter ]

00:09:04.734 --> 00:09:06.834
Yep, National Drink Beer Day,

00:09:06.834 --> 00:09:09.133
and, of course, for all those
who don't celebrate,

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:10.534
there's Coors Light.

00:09:10.534 --> 00:09:12.534
Yeah.
[ Laughter, scattered applause ]

00:09:12.534 --> 00:09:16.200
Let's get to some news.
Thank you.

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.200
Well, guys, today,
former president Trump

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:20.601
said that the war
between Russia and Ukraine

00:09:20.601 --> 00:09:22.734
would have never happened
if he were in office.

00:09:22.734 --> 00:09:25.000
And even --

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.367
He even offered to lead peace
talks between the two countries.

00:09:29.367 --> 00:09:32.234
Yeah, Trump said, "I'm an expert
on foreign affairs.

00:09:32.234 --> 00:09:34.467
I've had affairs
with many foreigners.

00:09:34.467 --> 00:09:37.033
[ Laughter ]

00:09:37.033 --> 00:09:39.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:41.167 --> 00:09:43.033
I should talk."

00:09:43.033 --> 00:09:45.367
Speaking of Trump,
according to a new book,

00:09:45.367 --> 00:09:47.067
at one point
during his presidency,

00:09:47.067 --> 00:09:50.367
he nearly fired Ivanka and Jared
over Twitter.

00:09:50.367 --> 00:09:53.968
[ Laughter ]

00:09:53.968 --> 00:09:56.100
Meanwhile, Eric and Don Jr.
were like, "Wait a minute.

00:09:56.100 --> 00:09:57.601
He follows you guys on Twitter?"

00:09:57.601 --> 00:09:59.267
[ Laughter ]

00:09:59.267 --> 00:10:00.534
Well, listen to this.

00:10:00.534 --> 00:10:01.734
Apparently Democratic insiders
are impressed with

00:10:01.734 --> 00:10:04.701
Gavin Newsom's
recent criticism of Republicans,

00:10:04.701 --> 00:10:07.267
and some think that he's
gearing up to run for president.

00:10:07.267 --> 00:10:09.567
[ Cheering, booing ]

00:10:09.567 --> 00:10:10.734
It's int-- Ooh.

00:10:10.734 --> 00:10:12.334
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.334 --> 00:10:14.667
-Meow!
-Yeah, that was great.

00:10:14.667 --> 00:10:17.868
It was like -- 'Cause everyone
was on this side of the crowd,

00:10:17.868 --> 00:10:20.334
and then -- Just very odd, yeah.

00:10:20.334 --> 00:10:21.634
I think it's just
very interesting,

00:10:21.634 --> 00:10:24.234
'cause if you put Newsom
in one of those aging apps,

00:10:24.234 --> 00:10:26.501
you pretty much get Joe Biden.

00:10:26.501 --> 00:10:27.968
And I just thought
that's very interesting.

00:10:27.968 --> 00:10:29.100
Very similar.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:30.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:30.534 --> 00:10:32.100
A little tweak up.

00:10:32.100 --> 00:10:34.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:34.501 --> 00:10:36.367
Hey, guys, I heard that Kia

00:10:36.367 --> 00:10:39.868
recalled 70,000 Sorento
and Sportage S.U.V.s

00:10:39.868 --> 00:10:41.901
after multiple reports of fires

00:10:41.901 --> 00:10:44.133
and localized melting incidents.

00:10:44.133 --> 00:10:46.033
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:46.033 --> 00:10:47.634
Kia was like,
"Look, on the bright side,

00:10:47.634 --> 00:10:49.400
you now have the world's biggest
panini maker."

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.167
So that's pretty good.
I mean...

00:10:52.167 --> 00:10:55.868
Apparently, the tow hitch
in the back could melt.

00:10:55.868 --> 00:10:58.601
My question is, who's towing
something with a Kia?

00:10:58.601 --> 00:10:59.901
[ Laughter ]

00:10:59.901 --> 00:11:02.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:06.033
"Want me to move
that tricycle for you?

00:11:06.033 --> 00:11:07.767
Hook her up to the back.
Let's go.

00:11:07.767 --> 00:11:10.067
Move that --
Let's go, ant.

00:11:10.067 --> 00:11:13.033
Let's go.
We're gonna go down the..."

00:11:13.033 --> 00:11:14.734
Well, get this --
McDonald's just announced

00:11:14.734 --> 00:11:16.667
that they're going to
start selling Happy Meals

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:18.067
with toys for adults.

00:11:18.067 --> 00:11:21.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:23.734
♪♪

00:11:23.734 --> 00:11:27.067
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.067 --> 00:11:29.167
Yep.
Happy Meals with adult toys.

00:11:29.167 --> 00:11:30.868
What could possibly go wrong?

00:11:30.868 --> 00:11:33.234
[ Laughter ]

00:11:33.234 --> 00:11:34.634
Some more business news.

00:11:34.634 --> 00:11:36.367
For the first time in 10 years,

00:11:36.367 --> 00:11:39.901
M&amp;M'S are adding a new character
to the mix, a purple peanut M&amp;M.

00:11:39.901 --> 00:11:41.067
Here she is.

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:43.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:43.767 --> 00:11:46.701
Yeah.
A purple peanut M&amp;M.

00:11:46.701 --> 00:11:49.434
Yeah, I guess the blue and red
M&amp;M'S date went really well.

00:11:49.434 --> 00:11:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:11:52.801 --> 00:11:53.901
♪♪

00:11:53.901 --> 00:11:56.334
-Adult toys.
-Alright, alright.

00:11:56.334 --> 00:11:59.000
-That's not Grimace.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.501
[ Rimshot ]

00:12:00.501 --> 00:12:03.634
-Switching gears,

00:12:03.634 --> 00:12:07.100
Pokémon just unveiled
a new character called Wiglett.

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.567
Take a look at this.

00:12:08.567 --> 00:12:11.467
[ Laughter ]

00:12:13.901 --> 00:12:16.234
That's one of the toys
in the adult Happy Meal.

00:12:16.234 --> 00:12:17.334
Yeah, that's exactly right.
Yeah.

00:12:17.334 --> 00:12:20.167
-Oh, my God.
-Did you guys see this?

00:12:20.167 --> 00:12:21.667
Last night at a concert in D.C.,

00:12:21.667 --> 00:12:23.934
Lizzo played
a never-used crystal flute

00:12:23.934 --> 00:12:26.434
that once belonged
to President James Madison.

00:12:26.434 --> 00:12:27.534
-Ooh!

00:12:27.534 --> 00:12:29.767
-No one had played it
in 200 years.

00:12:29.767 --> 00:12:32.601
So it was about damn time.
There you go.

00:12:32.601 --> 00:12:34.033
♪♪

00:12:35.267 --> 00:12:38.000
New York City
is buzzing tonight because

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:41.701
last night in Toronto,
Yankees superstar Aaron Judge

00:12:41.701 --> 00:12:44.400
hit his 61st home run
of the season,

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:48.167
tying Roger Maris'
American League record.

00:12:49.234 --> 00:12:51.400
Yep, Aaron Judge
did the impossible.

00:12:51.400 --> 00:12:54.634
He made non-Yankee fans
root for the Yankees.

00:12:54.634 --> 00:12:55.834
It was a special moment.

00:12:55.834 --> 00:12:57.367
New Yorkers haven't
cheered like this since

00:12:57.367 --> 00:12:58.701
Bill de Blasio left office.

00:12:58.701 --> 00:13:00.467
It was really amazing.

00:13:00.467 --> 00:13:03.100
Fans waited 61 years for
this to happen.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:06.267
That's right -- six decades of
waiting for one exciting moment.

00:13:06.267 --> 00:13:09.467
That sums up baseball
pretty well.

00:13:09.467 --> 00:13:11.334
It was a historic night
for Aaron Judge,

00:13:11.334 --> 00:13:13.467
and you could tell the announcer
was pretty excited,

00:13:13.467 --> 00:13:15.200
but I'm not sure about his
home-run call.

00:13:15.200 --> 00:13:16.334
Take a listen to this.

00:13:16.334 --> 00:13:19.300
-Swung on
and drilled deep left field.

00:13:19.300 --> 00:13:20.968
It is gone!

00:13:20.968 --> 00:13:23.033
He's done it! Move over, 69!

00:13:23.033 --> 00:13:25.901
The new hot thing to do
in the bedroom is 61!

00:13:25.901 --> 00:13:28.400
Its bom to the bom-bom.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:31.434
He's rounding the bases
like a senior on prom night!

00:13:31.434 --> 00:13:33.567
He's about to hear something
I never heard from my dad,

00:13:33.567 --> 00:13:36.334
which is,
"I'm proud of you, Son."

00:13:36.334 --> 00:13:38.634
Man, oh, man,
that ball left faster

00:13:38.634 --> 00:13:40.634
than my wife with the pool boy.

00:13:40.634 --> 00:13:42.567
Oh, baby!

00:13:42.567 --> 00:13:45.167
-He had weeks to practice that.

00:13:45.167 --> 00:13:47.200
Wasn't even appropriate,
I thought.

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:48.634
-Very emotional for him.
-Yeah.

00:13:48.634 --> 00:13:51.133
I thought -- Of course, a lot of
people went from the game

00:13:51.133 --> 00:13:52.934
hoping to catch
the home-run ball.

00:13:52.934 --> 00:13:54.868
You go the game, "Oh, my gosh.
If I catch this..."

00:13:54.868 --> 00:13:56.767
It was worth a
quarter of a million dollars

00:13:56.767 --> 00:13:57.901
if you caught the ball.

00:13:57.901 --> 00:13:59.868
And one guy came pretty close.

00:13:59.868 --> 00:14:01.601
Here he is. Look at this.

00:14:01.601 --> 00:14:05.701
Look at --
Less than 1 foot away.

00:14:05.701 --> 00:14:07.434
Yeah. Yeah. Oh, my gosh.

00:14:07.434 --> 00:14:08.968
And then every guy
who showed up to the game with

00:14:08.968 --> 00:14:11.467
a fishing net was like,
"Well, who's laughing now?"

00:14:12.167 --> 00:14:13.901
And get this -- the guy --
This is real.

00:14:13.901 --> 00:14:16.334
The guy who almost caught
the ball was a Toronto Blue Jays

00:14:16.334 --> 00:14:20.434
fan named -- and this is real --
Frankie Lasagna.

00:14:22.601 --> 00:14:24.000
-What?
-Yeah.

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:25.434
-Frankie Lasagna?

00:14:25.434 --> 00:14:27.868
-Frankie Lasagna
is that fan right there, yeah.

00:14:27.868 --> 00:14:29.801
Frankie Lasagna -- it sounds
like a name you get from

00:14:29.801 --> 00:14:33.167
the Olive Garden
Witness Protection Program.

00:14:33.167 --> 00:14:35.367
Frankie Lasagna sounds like
the name Robert De Niro

00:14:35.367 --> 00:14:37.400
checks into hotels
to avoid paparazzi.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.534
He's like...
-Hey!

00:14:39.534 --> 00:14:42.000
-Frankie Lasagna sounds like
the name of Trump's next lawyer.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.767
He's like, "Frankie Lasagna
is the greatest."

00:14:47.133 --> 00:14:48.701
Speaking of Trump,
it was just revealed

00:14:48.701 --> 00:14:50.667
that during the
FBI search of Mar-a-Lago,

00:14:50.667 --> 00:14:53.868
they seized 200,000 pages
of documents

00:14:53.868 --> 00:14:55.267
from the former president.

00:14:55.267 --> 00:14:57.100
200,000 pages.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.968
He's like a grandpa
who prints every e-mail.

00:14:58.968 --> 00:15:01.000
He's like...

00:15:01.000 --> 00:15:03.267
Yeah, if the FBI delayed
their search another day,

00:15:03.267 --> 00:15:06.000
the TV show "Hoarders"
would have beat them to it.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.133
Some more news.

00:15:07.133 --> 00:15:09.467
I read the Nord Stream
pipelines,

00:15:09.467 --> 00:15:11.467
which funnel
gas from Russia to Europe,

00:15:11.467 --> 00:15:14.200
has started leaking
due to underwater explosions.

00:15:14.200 --> 00:15:17.534
And the U.S. and Europe think
that Russia is responsible.

00:15:17.534 --> 00:15:19.534
-Ooh!
-Yeah, a leaky pipeline.

00:15:19.534 --> 00:15:20.701
Today, President Biden was like,

00:15:20.701 --> 00:15:22.934
"Oh, I have a
great urologist for that."

00:15:25.100 --> 00:15:26.167
Hey, guys, listen to this.

00:15:26.167 --> 00:15:27.534
A new poll shows that
more Democrats

00:15:27.534 --> 00:15:30.701
are now saying they want Biden
to run for re-election,

00:15:30.701 --> 00:15:32.667
and if he doesn't,
Vice President Harris

00:15:32.667 --> 00:15:33.868
is their top choice.

00:15:33.868 --> 00:15:37.234
That poll was conducted
among two people --

00:15:37.234 --> 00:15:39.400
Joe Biden and Kamala Harris.

00:15:44.467 --> 00:15:46.300
Meanwhile,
I saw that Bernie Sanders

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.501
is leaving the door open
for another presidential run

00:15:48.501 --> 00:15:49.801
in 2024.

00:15:49.801 --> 00:15:52.100
He'll be 83 years old.

00:15:52.100 --> 00:15:53.567
When other members of
the House heard about this,

00:15:53.567 --> 00:15:54.868
they had some thoughts.

00:15:54.868 --> 00:15:57.501
For example, first up,
Congressman Ken Buck said...

00:16:03.634 --> 00:16:06.133
Next up,
Congressman Jim Banks said...

00:16:12.667 --> 00:16:14.667
And Congressman
Tom Cotton said...

00:16:19.200 --> 00:16:21.634
And Congressman Colin Allred
said...

00:16:26.367 --> 00:16:28.801
And Congressman Virginia Foxx
said...

00:16:34.467 --> 00:16:36.701
And Congressman Dusty Johnson
said...

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.434
"My full name."
-His full name.

00:16:50.434 --> 00:16:53.167
♪♪
Oy!

00:16:53.167 --> 00:16:55.200
-And, finally,
Senator Roy Blunt said...

00:16:59.934 --> 00:17:01.133
There you go.

00:17:01.133 --> 00:17:02.701
Well, guys,
there's a lot of buzz around

00:17:02.701 --> 00:17:04.133
the new horror movie "Smile."

00:17:04.133 --> 00:17:05.601
Did you hear about this movie?

00:17:05.601 --> 00:17:07.634
Everybody -- This is going to be
the big movie this weekend.

00:17:07.634 --> 00:17:09.067
It's expected to be
such a big hit,

00:17:09.067 --> 00:17:12.067
they're already planning on
making a franchise out of it.

00:17:12.067 --> 00:17:13.968
Yeah, take a look at
the trailer I just saw.

00:17:13.968 --> 00:17:17.534
-This Friday, don't miss
the premiere of "Smile,"

00:17:17.534 --> 00:17:20.300
and then be sure to catch all
the heart-stopping sequels...

00:17:37.868 --> 00:17:39.367
-Wow. Very interesting.

00:17:39.367 --> 00:17:41.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:17:44.534 --> 00:17:45.701
Well, some business news.

00:17:45.701 --> 00:17:47.567
I saw that Hefty
just released new

00:17:47.567 --> 00:17:50.334
pumpkin-spice-scented
trash bags.

00:17:50.334 --> 00:17:52.200
Right now,
all the raccoons are like,

00:17:52.200 --> 00:17:54.300
"I know it's basic,
but I still love it, okay?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.767
Can I just say?"

00:17:55.767 --> 00:17:56.801
Well, this is interesting.

00:17:56.801 --> 00:17:58.501
According to new research,

00:17:58.501 --> 00:18:02.367
the pandemic may have changed
people's personalities forever.

00:18:02.367 --> 00:18:04.434
I'm not sure I've noticed anyone
acting differently.

00:18:04.434 --> 00:18:06.000
I mean, what about you, Higgins?

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.334
-Wouldn't know about that, Jack.
[ Jazz music playing ]

00:18:09.334 --> 00:18:11.901
I've always been the same.
Take it from Baccarat Steve.

00:18:11.901 --> 00:18:13.701
All Baccarat Steve
has ever cared about is

00:18:13.701 --> 00:18:16.033
the click, click, clickedy-clack
of the roulette wheel,

00:18:16.033 --> 00:18:17.167
seeing those triple cherries

00:18:17.167 --> 00:18:18.767
come up on
my favorite slot machine,

00:18:18.767 --> 00:18:22.100
and shoplifting crab legs from
Circus Circus buffet.

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.701
Mwah! Come on! Lucky 4s.

00:18:30.701 --> 00:18:33.400
-Quest, have you noticed Higgins
has been acting differently?

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.901
-[ Chuckles ]
[ Rock music playing ]

00:18:34.901 --> 00:18:37.667
I don't pay mind
to anybody but me,

00:18:37.667 --> 00:18:39.701
my leather jacket, and my Hog.

00:18:39.701 --> 00:18:40.734
[ Chuckles ]

00:18:40.734 --> 00:18:43.367
She's a '78 Harley Shovelhead,

00:18:43.367 --> 00:18:45.801
and there's nothing more
than I love in life

00:18:45.801 --> 00:18:48.434
than a little whipping her down
the South Dakota prairie,

00:18:48.434 --> 00:18:51.067
hitting 80 miles per hour
while the old lady

00:18:51.067 --> 00:18:55.434
sits behind and feeds me
meatballs from Olive Garden.

00:19:00.834 --> 00:19:02.501
-James, do you think
people's personalities

00:19:02.501 --> 00:19:04.367
changed because of the pandemic?

00:19:04.367 --> 00:19:06.634
-You know me, Jimmy.

00:19:06.634 --> 00:19:10.400
I've always been the same,
a fan of all things

00:19:10.400 --> 00:19:13.167
science fic--
[ Laughter ]

00:19:13.167 --> 00:19:16.534
Science fiction
and geek culture.

00:19:16.534 --> 00:19:19.234
I'm the biggest fan
of "House of the Dragon"

00:19:19.234 --> 00:19:23.634
this side of Westeros, LOL.

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:27.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:35.000
I've even learned
the language spoken

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:37.968
by the elves on the show,
High Valyrian.

00:19:37.968 --> 00:19:39.834
Check this out.
[ Clears throat ]

00:20:47.901 --> 00:20:49.901
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:20:54.801 --> 00:20:57.367
-What?
-I had no idea.

00:20:57.367 --> 00:21:01.200
-Okay. Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:21:01.200 --> 00:21:03.133
-Thank you, James.
-Wow, I guess.

00:21:03.133 --> 00:21:04.667
-I don't know.
-Wow, man.

00:21:04.667 --> 00:21:06.634
-That's odd.
-Wow.

00:21:08.701 --> 00:21:11.701
Finally...
[ Laughter ]

00:21:11.701 --> 00:21:13.601
...a new survey
found that over a quarter --

00:21:13.601 --> 00:21:17.067
I should let everyone at home
know that James

00:21:17.067 --> 00:21:20.100
never saw those cue cards or
wore that wig until just now.

00:21:20.100 --> 00:21:21.200
He had no idea.

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:24.133
We just surprised him
on the spot.

00:21:24.133 --> 00:21:26.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:21:32.400 --> 00:21:35.667
Finally, a new survey found
that over a quarter of Americans

00:21:35.667 --> 00:21:37.834
have been so hangry
that they've actually

00:21:37.834 --> 00:21:39.434
eaten out of the garbage.

00:21:39.434 --> 00:21:41.968
The most common explanation
they gave,

00:21:41.968 --> 00:21:44.467
"For some reason, the trash bags
smell like pumpkin spice."

00:21:45.634 --> 00:21:47.067
Well, this is nice.

00:21:47.067 --> 00:21:49.534
Today, President Biden hosted
The White House's first-ever

00:21:49.534 --> 00:21:52.767
Rosh Hashanah party to celebrate
the Jewish new year.

00:21:52.767 --> 00:21:56.534
Yeah. I think Biden was confused
because he ended his speech

00:21:56.534 --> 00:21:59.400
by saying, "Now let's watch
Ryan Seacrest do the countdown."

00:21:59.400 --> 00:22:01.567
And you go, "No."

00:22:01.567 --> 00:22:03.100
Yeah, they celebrated today,

00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:06.300
even though Rosh Hashanah
was Monday.

00:22:06.300 --> 00:22:08.701
That's like setting off
fireworks on the Ninth of July.

00:22:08.701 --> 00:22:11.100
You know what I'm saying?
It's fun, but is it...

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:13.133
But it was a nice party,
although it got awkward when

00:22:13.133 --> 00:22:14.734
Biden was
offered challah and said,

00:22:14.734 --> 00:22:17.367
"You want me to speak louder?

00:22:17.367 --> 00:22:19.968
I want that bread
you're holding.

00:22:19.968 --> 00:22:22.434
Holla at your boy, Jack."

00:22:24.267 --> 00:22:26.868
Then, a few hours later, the
president hosted a reception for

00:22:26.868 --> 00:22:28.934
Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:22:28.934 --> 00:22:30.534
Biden's staff was like,
"Hey, might as well

00:22:30.534 --> 00:22:32.334
knock out all
the cringey gaffes in one day.

00:22:32.334 --> 00:22:34.300
You know what I'm saying?"

00:22:34.300 --> 00:22:36.067
Biden held events
for the Jewish New Year

00:22:36.067 --> 00:22:37.834
and Hispanic Heritage Month.

00:22:37.834 --> 00:22:39.901
Staffers watched Biden the way
Aaron Judge's mom

00:22:39.901 --> 00:22:41.367
nervously watches his at bats.

00:22:41.367 --> 00:22:42.834
Like, "Come on, buddy.
You can do this.

00:22:42.834 --> 00:22:44.701
You can do this. Don't mess..."

00:22:44.701 --> 00:22:47.300
Meanwhile today,
Putin illegally claimed

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:49.701
four regions of Ukraine
as part of Russia.

00:22:49.701 --> 00:22:51.834
And to celebrate,
Putin and a few other leaders

00:22:51.834 --> 00:22:53.000
had a pretty
interesting handshake.

00:22:53.000 --> 00:22:54.067
Take a look at this.

00:22:54.067 --> 00:22:56.067
[ Applause ]

00:22:59.868 --> 00:23:02.634
-Oh!
[ Laughter ]

00:23:05.968 --> 00:23:08.400
-What?
-Oh!

00:23:08.400 --> 00:23:09.501
-Rest easy, Russia.

00:23:09.501 --> 00:23:12.400
That guy's
coordinating your war.

00:23:12.400 --> 00:23:13.934
That handshake looked like
a sandwich

00:23:13.934 --> 00:23:15.734
made up of tiny white sausages,
didn't it?

00:23:15.734 --> 00:23:18.234
-Ew!
-Well, this is big.

00:23:18.234 --> 00:23:19.901
Earlier tonight,
Elon Musk hosted

00:23:19.901 --> 00:23:21.868
Tesla's
Artificial Intelligence Day,

00:23:21.868 --> 00:23:24.501
and he was expected to
unveil Tesla Bot,

00:23:24.501 --> 00:23:26.334
a humanoid robot
designed to help with

00:23:26.334 --> 00:23:27.901
boring, repetitive tasks,

00:23:27.901 --> 00:23:30.033
stuff that humans
don't want to do anymore.

00:23:30.033 --> 00:23:31.567
For example, Tesla Bot can...

00:23:33.133 --> 00:23:34.667
or it can...

00:23:36.100 --> 00:23:37.701
It can...

00:23:40.901 --> 00:23:42.000
Then it can...

00:24:28.400 --> 00:24:30.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:24:31.934 --> 00:24:34.400
-Wow!

00:24:34.400 --> 00:24:36.467
[ Laughter ]

00:24:36.467 --> 00:24:37.567
-Some movie news.

00:24:37.567 --> 00:24:39.501
Today, 29 years after
the original,

00:24:39.501 --> 00:24:42.767
"Hocus Pocus 2"
premiered on Disney+.

00:24:42.767 --> 00:24:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:24:44.934 --> 00:24:46.133
The movie looks great.

00:24:46.133 --> 00:24:47.801
It's about three witches
who come back to life

00:24:47.801 --> 00:24:50.534
after Lizzo starts playing
a 200-year-old flute.

00:24:50.534 --> 00:24:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:24:55.200 --> 00:24:56.634
Hey, did you guys see this?

00:24:56.634 --> 00:24:59.501
Tomorrow is former president
Jimmy Carter's 98th birthday.

00:24:59.501 --> 00:25:01.267
-Ooh!
-Yeah, and this is exciting.

00:25:01.267 --> 00:25:02.901
He's also going to run
for a second term.

00:25:02.901 --> 00:25:05.467
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:25:05.467 --> 00:25:07.267
It's always nice to
hear about a famous Jimmy

00:25:07.267 --> 00:25:10.567
who doesn't host a
late-night talk show, isn't it?

00:25:10.567 --> 00:25:12.834
And, finally, I read that a
group of paleontologists

00:25:12.834 --> 00:25:16.133
just found fish teeth
that are 14 million years older

00:25:16.133 --> 00:25:19.100
than any teeth
found from any other species.

00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:21.367
We actually got in contact with
the paleontologists

00:25:21.367 --> 00:25:22.767
responsible for the find.

00:25:22.767 --> 00:25:24.434
Here's what they had to say.
The first one said...

00:25:27.000 --> 00:25:28.100
This next one said...

00:25:34.467 --> 00:25:36.067
And, finally,
the last scientist said...

00:25:45.968 --> 00:25:47.133
I'm really happy for those guys.

